prompt:
A real photograph of the inside of a small neighbourhood café in Berlin on a weekday morning, taken as a guest at the next table would take it with a good phone camera, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, soft morning daylight from a large window on the left. The textures of real wood, ceramic, glass, linen, bread, fabric and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young man from the front, the second in three-quarter view: his face, his short hair, his build and his height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; his clothes here are a dark-green sweater over a white T-shirt.

THE TABLE fills the lower half of the picture: a square light-wood café table seen from slightly above, with the young man sitting on the far side of it, facing the camera, and an empty wooden chair on the near right, pulled out a little. Every object on the table stands on its own, with a little bare wood around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. All the surfaces are plain: the jar, the cups, the jug and the plates carry no label, no print and no writing.

On the table, from the left of the picture to the right:
- a white coffee cup on its saucer, full of black coffee, with a teaspoon lying on the saucer;
- a small white milk jug and a white sugar bowl with its lid;
- in the middle, a white breakfast plate with a cut bread roll, a slice of cheese and two slices of ham, and a knife and a fork lying on either side of the plate;
- a white egg cup holding one brown boiled egg;
- a small glass jar of red strawberry jam with no label, next to a little dish with a block of butter;
- a tall glass of orange juice and a glass of water;
- a folded white paper napkin;
- a small glass vase with one yellow flower;
- a pair of plain white salt and pepper shakers;
- a closed menu with a plain dark-green cover, lying flat at the edge of the table;
- the young man's phone, lying face down.

THE YOUNG MAN of the reference pictures sits on the far side of the table, seen from the waist up above the table top. He is caught in the middle of his breakfast: he holds the coffee cup in one hand just above the saucer, and his face is turned up towards the waitress with a half-smile that reaches his eyes. His other hand rests on the table beside the plate. His dark-blue backpack hangs on the back of his chair, and his grey jacket hangs over the back of the empty chair on the near right.

THE WAITRESS stands at the right-hand side of the table, seen from the knees up: a woman of about forty with short curly grey hair and glasses, in a black shirt and a long dark-brown apron. She is setting down a small white plate with a slice of apple cake on it at the right-hand corner of the table, and looking at the young man as she does so. Her other hand holds nothing.

THE CAFÉ behind them, from the left of the picture to the right:
- on the left, the large window with a white frame, the street in soft light behind the glass, and a green plant in a pot on the windowsill;
- in the middle, a wooden counter with a glass cake dome on it, under which stand a round chocolate cake and a fruit tart, and behind the counter a silver coffee machine and a few white cups stacked on top of it;
- on the right, the open door of the café, and next to it a coat hook on the wall with one red scarf hanging from it;
- above the counter, two round lamps with white glass shades hang from the ceiling;
- at a small table in the back, an older man with a white beard sits alone with a cup of tea, his teapot beside it, looking out of the window.

The walls are painted a warm pale yellow, the floor is old wooden boards, and nothing on the walls carries any writing.
